at are hell-bent on indoctrinating my kids and your kids and all the rest of the kids. And I would replace them with teachers. that are willing to, you know, teach them every single, every single side of the issue, including American history and teaching our kids that, you know, though the United States of America is not perfect, it is a pretty amazing place and we're all blessed and fortunate to live here. So that's, if I could, if I could make a, you know, one change for my kids, that's probably what I do. All right, I'll let you off the hook. And I think the last thing when you're talking about that is that our children have so much to do with the current state of things and where they're going to go. And I love the fact that you're talking about hearing both sides of the story. That's what this show is about. There's a reason why there's an elephant and a donkey on the logo. I'll fall on the Democrat side sometimes, and I'll say, hey, we reacted this way. But I appreciate that, Eli, I do. your message to the constituents of Arizona. They're going to watch this. They're going to start googling you and probably not this soon because most people don't get involved until, you know, about three or four months. But I would love to really hear what your message is to the Arizonans and then I'll wrap it up with some final thoughts and we'll let you get back to the family. Yeah, my message is this. The United States of America can only handle so",
